From: Proofloom Contributor <proofloom-contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:05:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add 50 more bundled language dictionaries (86 total)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The writing desk now checks spelling in 86 languages. 27 more languages
ship as locked dictionary-* npm packages; 23 languages that have no npm
package are vendored straight from the LibreOffice/dictionaries repository
(the same upstream the npm suite is generated from), fetched by
scripts/vendor-languages.mjs — the single table of record — during
npm run build, so the Pages workflow needs no extra steps. Fetched files
are gitignored and reproducible; offline builds skip them and still work.

New npm languages (27): Belarusian, Breton, Bosnian, Catalan (Valencia),
Welsh, Greek (Polytonic), Faroese, Friulian, West Frisian, Scottish
Gaelic, Armenian, Western Armenian, Interlingua, Interlingue, Interslavic,
Georgian, Latin, Luxembourgish, Latgalian, Macedonian, Mongolian, Low
German, Nepali, Occitan, Russian (Petrine orthography), Serbian (Latin
script), Turkmen.

Vendored LibreOffice languages (23): Afrikaans, Aragonese, Arabic,
Assamese, Bangla, Tibetan, Kurdish (Sorani), Gujarati, Guarani, Hindi,
Indonesian, Kurdish (Kurmanji), Kannada, Ligurian, Marathi, Odia,
Punjabi, Sanskrit, Sinhala, Albanian, Swahili, Tamil, Telugu.

- scripts/vendor-languages.mjs: vendored-language table with per-language
  licenses and upstream folders, plus idempotent fetchers for dictionary
  pairs (normalized index.aff/index.dic, verbatim license/readme files,
  manifest.json) and OpenSubtitles frequency lists (2018 dump, falling
  back to 2016 for 16 languages; variant codes share a base list).
- scripts/build.mjs: LANGUAGE_PACKS grows to 86 rows, vendor rows derive
  from the vendored table, per-language license/source metadata reads from
  it, and the frequency source label records the real dump version.
- scripts/fetch-frequency.sh: new codes + 2016 fallback for manual runs.
- Frequency-ranked suggestions now cover 50 of the 86 languages.
- package.json: 27 new locked dictionary-* dependencies.
- Docs (README, LANGUAGE_PACKS, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES) updated honestly:
  14M+ entries, per-suite license summaries, and a note that space-less
  scripts (Thai, Lao, Khmer) stay unbundled because the spelling pipeline
  segments on spaces.
- tests: Welsh/Latin/Vendored-Hindi/Vendored-Arabic check and correct
  real misspellings through LazyHunspell, variant-code mapping cases
  (hi-IN, ca-valencia, sr-Latn, el-Polyton), and the dist test now
  asserts the expanded set. dictionary-rw and dictionary-tlh were
  evaluated and rejected (mislabeled data; pIqaD private-use script the
  tokenizer cannot match).
